---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Home
description: A conference reference for Authentication for humans, why passkeys finally make sense.
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="site-shell hero-panel reveal">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ talk.project.event }}</p>
      <h1>{{ talk.project.title }}</h1>
      <p class="lede">Authentication keeps failing because we keep asking humans to manage reusable secrets in hostile environments. Passkeys point to a better deal: cryptographic proof, fewer passwords, and login flows that are less hostile to the people using them.</p>
      <p class="button-row">
        <a class="nav-button" href="{{ talk.slides[0] | slidePath | url }}">Start reading</a>
        <a class="nav-button" href="{{ '/resources/' | url }}">Browse resources</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="site-shell content-section" aria-labelledby="slide-index">
  <p class="eyebrow">After the session</p>
  <h2 id="slide-index">Follow the argument</h2>
  <p class="lede">Read it in order, or jump to the part you want to revisit. Each page keeps the slide, the explanation, and the references together.</p>
  <div class="slide-grid">
    {% for slide in talk.slides %}
      <article class="source-card slide-card">
        <img src="{{ slide | slideAsset | url }}" alt="Slide {{ slide.number }}: {{ slide.title }}" loading="lazy">
        <p class="type">Slide {{ slide.number }}</p>
        <h3><a href="{{ slide | slidePath | url }}">{{ slide.title }}</a></h3>
        <p>{{ slide.page_summary }}</p>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
